the tree.\"\n- `config_key::verify.plan_review_engine` has no entry in `.github/mechanism-baseline.json`. The baseline has no write path for new keys (drain_stale only keeps existing ones; no --lock), and AGENTS.md forbids hand-editing it.\n- So the plan's step 1 makes `check_mechanism_delta.py --check` and `make verify` fail. \"Permanent, names no ticket\" conflicts with the ratchet policy, and no wording-only change can satisfy both. The same applies to closing bossy-impish-hoiho, which the close precheck refuses while the marker names it.\nThis is an operator decision, so the plan is unchanged and the ticket unclaimed.","timestamp":1794535656331386386},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator direction, 2026-11-12: `[verify] plan_review_engine` is a first-class setting and must follow the conventions the other settings use. For the mechanism ratchet, that means a `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` entry: 104 other `config_key`/`feature_flag` settings are admitted this way, and 3 are admitted by markers. The operator authorizes adding this one entry and removing the sunset marker. That resolves the blocker the earlier plan review raised (a reason with no ticket fails `sunset_markers.py`). The description has been rewritten to match. The environment-variable exclusion stays, per the ADR 0123 operator decision of 2026-11-09.","timestamp":1794539867121137382},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Correction to the previous comment and to plan step 1: the operator said this key is first-class and should follow the settings conventions. The operator has NOT yet explicitly authorized editing `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` by hand, which AGENTS.md forbids for contributors. Admitting the key through the baseline was the coordinator's reading of that direction. Do not edit the baseline until the operator explicitly authorizes it; an authorization will be recorded here as a separate comment.","timestamp":1794539882039739492},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator direction, 2026-11-12: follow the repo's established conventions. That supersedes both earlier comments on this ticket. The baseline is not edited by hand.\n\nPer docs/architecture.md §\"Mechanism-delta ratchet\" and sunset_markers.py, a mechanism added after the baseline froze is admitted only by a marker that names an open ticket. For a permanent setting, that ticket is the standing admission ticket cankered-cloistered-bittern (7447-47d8-051d-42ab). It is not part of the epic, so the epic can still close. The description now says to repoint the marker at that ticket.","timestamp":1794540417182715289},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-12: plan review PASS (Bedrock, 5 advisories: grep AC is a judgment over src; obsolete needs --reason, which the coordinator's command supplies). Claimed. Worktree .rebar/worktrees/engine-permanent, commit 7f163dae688 (Change-Id Id8ca135831470c0fdc3b2f9ce43a056188413b46): marker now '# mechanism-ok: config_key verify.plan_review_engine — 7447-47d8-051d-42ab (ADR 0123)'; sunset wording dropped in _config_sources.py and rebar.toml; ADR 0123 Lifetime and Consequences rewritten plus a dated 2026-11-12 amendment. check_mechanism_delta --check exits 0; .github/mechanism-baseline.json unchanged; the AC grep filtered to engine/hoiho/0123 lines prints nothing; docs/config.md, docs/plan-review-gate.md and docs/cli-reference.md had no sunset wording, so they are unchanged. make verify running.","timestamp":1794541393712975001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"make verify exit 0 at 7f163dae688: lint/typecheck clean, 21252 passed / 29 skipped (default tier), 218 passed / 2 skipped (integration tier). Pushed as Gerrit change 3389.","timestamp":1794543528708183001}],"created_at":1794534809163372698,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8dbb4a9f-4056-4a9d-b444-019d169259a2","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e557-4f22-2246-431f"},{"link_uuid":"909729df-8b67-4f8b-9fd3-1c0f0287cb17","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1227-04f2-5d70-4035"}],"description":"## Problem\n\n`[verify] plan_review_engine` is a first-class, permanent setting. Both plan-review engines, the 4-pass pipeline and the single read-only agent, stay supported, and this key selects between them (operator decision, 2026-11-12). It must follow the repo's established conventions.\n\nTwo things still treat it as temporary:\n- **Its mechanism-ratchet marker names a retirement ticket.** `src/rebar/_config_sections.py:57` reads `# mechanism-ok: config_key verify.plan_review_engine — bossy-impish-hoiho`. That ticket plans to retire an engine, which will not happen, and rebar refuses to close it while the marker names it.\n- **Wording calls it temporary:**\n  - `src/rebar/_config_sources.py:361`: \"The engine-switch sunset ticket removes the entry.\"\n  - `rebar.toml:34`: \"Sunset with the switch: bossy-impish-hoiho.\"\n  - `docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md:40-41`: the Lifetime bullet.\n  - `docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md:136`: the Consequences bullet.\n\n**Convention for admitting a mechanism added after the baseline froze** (`docs/architecture.md` §\"Mechanism-delta ratchet\"; `src/rebar/_commands/sunset_markers.py`):\n- A contributor never hand-edits `.github/mechanism-baseline.json`.\n- A `# mechanism-ok:` marker at the definition site names a ticket, and that ticket stays open while the marker exists.\n- For a permanent setting, the named ticket is a standing admission ticket. That ticket is `cankered-cloistered-bittern` (`7447-47d8-051d-42ab`).\n\nThe key's documentation already follows the settings convention: a row in the generated `docs/config-reference.md`, an entry in the `docs/config.md` key inventory, `rebar.toml`, and `docs/plan-review-gate.md`.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. **Repoint the marker** at the standing admission ticket, keeping the marker grammar (a reason that opens with the ticket id):\n   `# mechanism-ok: config_key verify.plan_review_engine — 7447-47d8-051d-42ab permanent engine selection (ADR 0123)`\n   Do not edit `.github/mechanism-baseline.json`.\n2. **Reword the `_config_sources.py` comment.** The `_ENV_EXCLUDED_KEYS` entry is permanent: the key deliberately takes no environment override, per the ADR 0123 decision of 2026-11-09. That decision is unchanged.\n3. **Reword the `rebar.toml` comment** and drop its sunset clause.\n4. **Amend ADR 0123:**\n   - Replace the Lifetime bullet. It should say the key is permanent, both engines are supported, and the ratchet marker names the standing admission ticket `cankered-cloistered-bittern`.\n   - Reword the Consequences bullet to say both engines are maintained as supported options.\n   - Add a dated 2026-11-12 amendment note recording the change of intent.\n   - Keep the ADR status as Accepted.\n5. **Check the settings docs** (`docs/config.md`, `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/cli-reference.md`).\n   - Remove any sunset or retirement wording for this key.\n   - Match how sibling `verify.*` keys are documented.\n   - If `docs/config-reference.md` is affected, regenerate it with `scripts/gen_config_reference.py`; don't hand-edit it.\n\nNo behavior changes: the key, its `pipeline` default, both engines, and the environment-variable exclusion all stay as they are.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The marker for `verify.plan_review_engine` names `7447-47d8-051d-42ab`, and `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` is unchanged.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] `git grep -n -iE 'bossy-impish-hoiho|sunset' -- src rebar.toml docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md docs/config.md docs/plan-review-gate.md docs/cli-reference.md` prints no line about the engine switch.\n- [ ] ADR 0123 states that the key is permanent and both engines are supported, names the standing admission ticket, and carries a dated 2026-11-12 amendment note.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] After the change merges, `bossy-impish-hoiho` is closed with `--class obsolete`, and the command and its output are recorded in a comment on this ticket.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_config_sections.py","reason":"marker reason"},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_sources.py","reason":"comment wording"},{"path":"rebar.toml","reason":"comment wording"},{"path":"docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md","reason":"Lifetime, Consequences, amendment"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"sunset wording, if any"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"sunset wording, if any"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"],["relates_to","1227-04f2-5d70-4035"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"bdef8f1c-d4e5-474e-9a05-02dee1b19524","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"1bdc-d4f7-2160-4fda","ticket_type":"task","title":"Make the plan-review engine a first-class permanent setting","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["fc9e4c82-5c61-4ed2-9219-e7bed613a4d3","8dbb4a9f-4056-4a9d-b444-019d169259a2","f01ca7c4-fb0e-4b4a-8813-68d3badeec52","bea5baa4-d04c-4df1-90f3-4043338ee673","52fc3364-3bb7-43cf-9daa-dea93e7d0985","0a92f1dc-861a-4b2e-8079-04671c5575c8","9f6e777f-158c-4cfb-ad04-9027ce7bc623","d27ba2d1-9b85-425d-901d-47d6f54299c9","523c1109-5ef6-421c-9be9-70957534c0aa","1cc48707-a320-44ce-a70e-dd1a5221dfbe","4775bb78-f2a5-4cea-b510-b46b5610a371","bdef8f1c-d4e5-474e-9a05-02dee1b19524","7b42c52f-0643-41fc-a9ae-033734ac0720","0122d501-27d6-41a7-a18c-d871d1ea90f1","8e8b8aaa-4954-4633-88ef-49be3551d077","909729df-8b67-4f8b-9fd3-1c0f0287cb17"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794544091981306853,"uuid":"1e05a0b5-50fb-4857-b9f9-b609a53ed29c"}